@startuml f2-automation-submits-task
title F2 - Automation submits a task (publish to Router queue)

|Auto|
start
:Build task payload
 with prompt, tools, secret_ids;
:REST POST /tasks to Router
 with bearer_token and payload;

note right
  Router is the task queue manager.
  GW is not on the create path.
  The API Gateway, State Registry, and
  Secret Registry have no connection to Router.
  Auto publishes directly to Router.
end note

|Router|
:Receive task;
:Persist in Router DB
 with status=incoming;
:Enqueue in incoming list;
:Process via subscribed services
 (validate, build scope_token);
:Move processed task to executor wait list;
:Return 202 with task_id;

|Auto|
:Receive 202;
:Store task_id for later correlation;

stop

@enduml